CONTROL minimal-container W=8 collapses : True -> ok
CONTROL minimal-container W=7 does not  : True -> ok

wide container (always u64), widths where wrap == clamp : [64]
minimal container (u8/u16/u32/u64),      same           : [8, 16, 32, 64]

degenerate index points, wide arm    : 1 of 128
degenerate index points, minimal arm : 4 of 128

READING: the set of index points at which the overflow policy has no
         content is NOT a property of the declared width. It is a
         property of (declared width, container), and the container is
         chosen by the treatment. Changing the container policy moves
         the degenerate set from [64] to [8, 16, 32, 64].
